Short Description (approx. 130 words):
The Garden of Deception maps rhetorical stances—truth, uncertainty, refusal, contradiction, manipulation, deception, and strategy—into botanical growth rules. Each rule tunes turning, jitter, and branching to produce distinct morphologies that interact across a shared field. A ring motif around “deception” hints at gravitational pull and self‑referential loops, while restrained line weight and a minimal palette foreground structure over surface. Determinism via a fixed seed preserves the specific composition on display while the system itself remains generative. The piece explores how simple, legible parameters can yield complex form, echoing how narratives and tactics shape living systems over time.

